    "title": "The Sock Window",
    "passage": "Lily and Ben were putting clean socks into pairs. One blue sock was missing, although they had checked the washing basket twice. Ben looked under the table and behind the door. Lily picked up a white shirt from the basket and noticed something blue through the thin cloth. She put her hand inside a sleeve and pulled out the missing sock. Ben laughed and held up another shirt like a window. There was nothing inside that one, but he checked the rest before putting them down. Soon, every sock had a partner. Lily placed the last blue pair on top of the pile. Ben put the empty basket on his head for a moment. Lily told him to check it first, in case there was another sock hiding inside.",
